 "final_passage": "On the unseen Banking and Travel test sets, Wrenfold achieved macro-F1 scores of 93.1% and 92.4%, respectively, outperforming Fennick-Base by 1.5 percentage points in each domain. However, because no statistical tests were reported, these differences are descriptive only and cannot be interpreted as significant. The evaluation was limited to the Banking and Travel domains, so the results do not provide evidence that Wrenfold's advantage generalizes to other domains. Both neural models outperformed the Keyword-SVM reference, with Wrenfold leading by 8.9 percentage points on each domain and Fennick-Base by 7.4 percentage points.",
